# Spicy Watermelon Margarita

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Salt or Tajín]{ ing="salt-or-taj-n" } (optional), for rim
- [ ] 1 wedge [lime]{ ing="lime" } (optional), for rim
- [ ] 1-2 [thin slices jalapeño]{ ing="thin-slices-jalape-o" } or serrano pepper
- [ ] 1-2 tsp [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] [Ice]{ ing="ice" }
- [ ] 2 oz fresh [watermelon juice]{ ing="watermelon-juice" }
- [ ] 1.5 oz [blanco tequila]{ ing="blanco-tequila" }
- [ ] 1 oz fresh [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }

## Recipe

1. Chill a cocktail glass.
1. If you want a salted rim: On a cutting board, make a small mound of salt/[Tajín]{ ing="salt-or-taj-n" }. Take the [lime]{ ing="lime" } and run the pulpy part of the fruit around the exterior rim of the cocktail glass, then gently roll the rim over the mound of salt so that the salt sticks to the lime-moistened edge. Set the glass aside.
1. In a cocktail shaker, muddle the slices of pepper in the [sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }. Fill the shaker with [ice]{ ing="ice" }, then add the [watermelon juice]{ ing="watermelon-juice" }, [tequila]{ ing="blanco-tequila" } and [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }. Shake hard for 30 seconds, then double-strain into the cocktail glass.
